{"title":"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Basic_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Basic Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Cassie leaves Escanaba at 8:30 AM heading for Marquette on her bike. She bikes at a uniform rate of 12 miles per hour. Brian leaves Marquette at 9:00 AM heading for Escanaba on his bike. He bikes at a uniform rate of 16 miles per hour. They both bike on the same 62-mile route between Escanaba and Marquette. At what time in the morning do they meet? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/508d8be44157bc4df8499cd01ef41e16a053a98b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10: 00\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10: 15\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 10: 30\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11: 00\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 11: 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"560\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Cassie leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> an hour earlier then Brian, when Brian starts, the distance between them will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7ee0ce218959a8183834c745a55ea5650d9fd9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62-\\frac{12}{2}=56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />. Every hour, they will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/4812588be093b90c9fe9705f5348b4f8bce83cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+16=28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> miles closer. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/98050623fe223b54b5b15ff6098cfed83bde8e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{56}{28}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />, so 2 hours from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/3817efc5c25969d2068ac5c6774a1ae6ba3181cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> AM is when they meet, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e98595be46b5f5cdcdfed74d39b86ecc649cb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11: 00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"98\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Basic_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Basic_Algebra)\">Solution 2 (Basic Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Basic Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the # of hours after Cassie leaves, when both of them meet. In that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> hours, Cassie will travel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/38588fafb659d83dc4c41024358d54ce788611d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> miles. But, Brian will travel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e663cce45b0dc5824593241d41c2f8c09c17c805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16(x-1/2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> miles as he starts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> hours after Cassie. These two distances sum to the total distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e67376d85a21889a01b76d7c9d8c765b2bac379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles as they meet here, yielding the equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bce506e4b2c9dc05dda6d3275547152ae9cf17c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x+16(x-1/2)=62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" />. After distribution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc14160c6586817bc3d3bb4bfa76d59c91b8ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x+16x-8=62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" />. After combining like terms and adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to both sides we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e7d00a523cdff223c3cd2f1102cf66ff5960ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28x=70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d855323d65b0c5eef448319cf572be9e93aca89d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />. So they meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aae3c8770ff05ef2072c00583640a2757187994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> hours after 8:30 a.m. which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e98595be46b5f5cdcdfed74d39b86ecc649cb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11: 00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"98\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>- LearnForEver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/EnpR7rjMYzg\">https://youtu.be/EnpR7rjMYzg</a> Soo, DRMS, NM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IomJc_tK0x4\">https://youtu.be/IomJc_tK0x4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 8\">2006 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problem